 - Must include either a `TicketSequence` or `Sequence` value greater than zero.
 
 {% admonition type="warning" name="Caution" %}
-A `Batch` transaction returns `tesSUCCESS` on the outer transaction even if some or all _inner_ transactions fail. To confirm that inner transactions succeeded, look up each transaction by its hash and check its own result and metadata. See [Metadata](../../../../concepts/transactions/batch-transactions.md#metadata) and [Check Batch transaction result](../../../../tutorials/best-practices/transaction-sending/send-a-single-account-batch-transaction.md#6-check-batch-transaction-result) to learn more.
+A `Batch` transaction returns `tesSUCCESS` on the outer transaction even if some or all _inner_ transactions fail. To confirm that inner transactions succeeded, look up each transaction by its hash and check its own result and metadata. With `tfAllOrNothing`, rolled-back inner transactions are not committed: their hashes can return `txnNotFound`, with no published inner failure code. Establish complete coverage of the outer transaction's validated ledger before interpreting missing inner hashes as a rollback. See [Metadata](../../../../concepts/transactions/batch-transactions.md#metadata) and [Check Batch transaction result](../../../../tutorials/best-practices/transaction-sending/send-a-single-account-batch-transaction.md#6-check-batch-transaction-result) to learn more.
